Brand logos in this folder (google, x, reddit, ycombinator, linkedin, youtube,
github, producthunt, facebook, instagram, duckduckgo, stripe, lemonsqueezy,
claude, perplexity, googlegemini, bluesky, threads, mastodon, tiktok,
pinterest, discord, telegram, whatsapp, substack, medium, devdotto, hashnode,
indiehackers, brave, ecosia, baidu, deepseek, kagi, qwant, startpage, googlechrome,
safari, firefoxbrowser, opera, apple, android, linux, anthropic, meta, bytedance, openrouter) are from Simple Icons, https://simpleicons.org, released under CC0 1.0
Universal. amazon is from Simple Icons 14.0.0. chatgpt (OpenAI) and slack are from Simple Icons 14.0.0, bing
(Microsoft Bing) from 12.0.0 and yahoo from 9.0.0, before those marks were
removed from the set; slack is recoloured in its four brand colours. google,
googlechrome, amazon and bytedance are split into their official brand
colours; bing, instagram, googlegemini, mastodon, firefoxbrowser, meta,
telegram and safari use their brand gradients; tiktok and youtube add their
second brand colour. duckduckgo and linux add their official beak, bow tie,
eye and feet colours under the one-colour mark, and copilot uses its brand
gradient. The trademarks belong to their owners.

copilot.svg is Microsoft's one-colour Copilot mark and yandex.svg is Yandex's
own icon, both as published on Wikimedia Commons. They and the marks above are
used only as small icons that identify a traffic source.

dodo.svg (Dodo Payments), polar.svg (Polar), creem.svg (Creem), revenuecat.svg
(RevenueCat), paddle.svg (Paddle), woocommerce.svg (WooCommerce) and shopify.svg
(Shopify) are those companies' own logos and trademarks, used only to identify
their payment services. woocommerce.svg is WooCommerce's purple circle icon
drawn with the W of its official logo.

lobsters.svg wraps the site's own icon from lobste.rs, used only as a small
icon that identifies a traffic source.

commoncrawl.svg is the mark from Common Crawl's own logo on commoncrawl.org,
used only as a small icon that identifies its crawler.

Flags in ../flags are from flag-icons, https://github.com/lipis/flag-icons,
